  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting evidence-informed and inclusive youth policymaking</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity will support Member States in addressing the exacerbated challenges caused by the poly-crises era on young people, through evidence-informed and inclusive youth policy-making. Using its Toolbox on Youth Policy and Programming, UNESCO will provide technical and policy guidance to national governments and stakeholders on how to develop and implement policies affecting youth with the meaningful engagement of youth at all stages of the process. In conjunction with other workstreams under the Youth Programme, UNESCO will also support the integration of relevant findings from youth-led/youth-relevant research into national policy processes, as well enable intergenerational dialogue and institutional capacity building on youth development and civic engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
